---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Fitness x Marketing handles website, newsletter, tool and Google notification data, and how to contact us about your privacy."
  canonical="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <article class="privacy-policy">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Fitness × Marketing</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 25 October 2026</p>
      <p>This policy explains how Fitness x Marketing, operated by Melisa Gjika in Tirana, Albania, handles information through this website, its tools, newsletter and the <strong>Fitness x Marketing Tool Notifications</strong> Google application.</p>
      <p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:gjikamelisa@gmail.com">gjikamelisa@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="contents" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <a href="#information">Information we handle</a>
      <a href="#google">Google notification app</a>
      <a href="#providers">Service providers</a>
      <a href="#choices">Your choices and requests</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="information">
      <h2>1. Information we handle and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Messages and enquiries.</strong> If you contact us, we receive your email address, the information in your message and any attachments. We use these to respond and provide the help you request.</li>
        <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions.</strong> When you subscribe, Kit processes your email address and subscription information to deliver emails and manage your subscription. Email delivery and engagement information may be used to understand how the newsletter is performing.</li>
        <li><strong>Tool submissions.</strong> The Ideal Client FAQ Finder processes quiz choices in your browser. When you submit an email address to unlock the report, it sends that address, your answers and the generated client profile to our lead system through Supabase. Answers include the audience characteristics and fitness goals you select. We use these details to provide the tool experience and manage related submissions and follow-up.</li>
        <li><strong>Call bookings.</strong> The booking page loads Calendly to display availability and collect the details you provide to schedule a call. Campaign parameters in the page URL are passed to Calendly. We measure booking page opens and completed bookings through Google Analytics. Calendly processes scheduling information under its own privacy policy.</li>
        <li><strong>Website usage.</strong> Google Analytics helps us understand visits, pages viewed and how people reach and use the site. Cloudflare serves the website. Our traffic logging integration sends request details to Profound for traffic and automated-agent analysis, including the page path, URL query parameters, IP address, browser information, referring page, time and response status.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some tools link to separate services, including ChatGPT, Instagram and Gumroad. Information you provide on those services is handled under their own privacy policies. Avoid entering identifiable client health information into forms or URLs; use anonymous examples when exploring coaching tools.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="google">
      <h2>2. Fitness x Marketing Tool Notifications</h2>
      <p>Fitness x Marketing Tool Notifications uses Google Apps Script to send tool-related notification emails through the Google account that authorizes the app. The email-sending permission is displayed by Google as “Send email as you”.</p>
      <p>For this function, the app handles the authorized sending account, configured recipient email addresses, and the subject and body of notification messages. A notification can contain information associated with a tool submission. This information is used to deliver the notification and support the related tool workflow.</p>
      <p>The send-email permission does not itself grant permission to read your inbox. Google handles account sign-in and authorization; you do not provide your Google password to Fitness x Marketing.</p>
      <p>Google processes the authorization and email delivery. Notification content is shared with the configured recipients and their email providers. Submission records and notification messages may also remain in the connected submission systems and email accounts used for that workflow. Revoking access stops future authorized access; it does not recall messages already delivered or automatically delete existing records.</p>
      <p>Data obtained through Google account permissions is used for the notification function and its support, not for advertising, sale to data brokers or training general-purpose AI models. We limit access to what is needed to operate the feature, investigate security issues or meet legal obligations. Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs is subject to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>
      <p>You can remove the app’s access in your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. To request deletion of records held by Fitness x Marketing, contact us using the email below.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="providers">
      <h2>3. Service providers and sharing</h2>
      <p>We use service providers to host the site, run tools, store submissions, deliver emails and understand traffic. Depending on the feature you use, these include Cloudflare, Google, Kit, Supabase, Profound and Calendly. Tool workflows may also use Make, Google Sheets and Telegram to transfer submissions, maintain records and notify the site operator.</p>
      <p>We share information needed for these functions and may disclose information where required by law or necessary to address abuse or security incidents. If you follow a link to buy a product through Gumroad, Gumroad handles the checkout and payment information under its own policies.</p>
      <p>These services may process information outside your country. Their processing locations and privacy terms depend on the service. You can contact us about a particular tool or submission if you need more detail.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>Google Analytics and embedded newsletter services can use cookies or similar technologies to measure visits and interactions. The Ideal Client FAQ Finder uses browser storage to limit repeated submissions. You can block or clear cookies and local storage in your browser, although some embedded features may work differently.</p>
      <p>Browser cookie settings do not prevent the server-side request logging described above. Google also provides an <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Retention and security</h2>
      <p>Information is retained for the purposes described here, including providing requested services, maintaining subscriptions, handling enquiries, troubleshooting and meeting applicable legal obligations. Retention varies by record type and service provider; there is no single retention period for all systems. Contact us to request deletion of a specific submission or account-related record.</p>
      <p>Copies already delivered to an email recipient, provider backups or records required for legal or security purposes may not be removed immediately. Access to operational accounts is restricted, and the website uses HTTPS. No internet service can guarantee complete security.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="choices">
      <h2>6. Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> use the unsubscribe link in an email to stop newsletter messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Google access:</strong> remove Fitness x Marketing Tool Notifications in your Google Account connections.</li>
        <li><strong>Your information:</strong> email <a href="mailto:gjikamelisa@gmail.com">gjikamelisa@gmail.com</a> to ask what information we hold about you, request a correction or deletion, or raise a privacy concern. Include the email address you used and the relevant tool, without sending passwords or unnecessary sensitive information.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Depending on applicable law, you may also have rights to access or receive a copy of your data, restrict or object to processing, withdraw consent, or complain to a data-protection authority. We may need to verify that a request relates to your information before acting on it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We will update this page when our practices change and revise the date above. If a change requires additional consent, including a new use of Google account data, we will seek that consent before the new use.</p>
    </section>

    <aside class="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Melisa Gjika · Fitness x Marketing<br />Tirana, Albania<br /><a href="mailto:gjikamelisa@gmail.com">gjikamelisa@gmail.com</a></p>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-policy { max-width: 740px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.04em; margin: .7rem 0 1rem; }
  .updated { color: #596371; font-size: .95rem; }
  .contents { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .65rem 1.3rem; padding: 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; background: var(--mint); border-left: 3px solid var(--deep-teal); }
  .privacy-policy a { color: #006d6b; text-underline-offset: .18em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  section { margin-top: 2.5rem; scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  li { margin-bottom: .85rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  .contact { margin-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--gray); padding-top: 1rem; }
</style>
